abstract: >-
  ZenBrain is an open-source agent memory library for LLM agents: seven
  neuroscience-inspired memory layers behind a memory coordinator that
  stores, recalls, forgets and consolidates, and a library of 20 algorithm
  modules (10 core, 10 advanced research modules) with FSRS spaced
  repetition, Hebbian learning, Ebbinghaus forgetting curves, emotional
  tagging, sleep replay, Bayesian confidence propagation and
  context-dependent retrieval. Which
  mechanisms the coordinator runs on its own and which the library offers
  as functions is listed in the repository README. TypeScript; the
  algorithm package has zero runtime dependencies.
